Z||000004||California Kid||09-23-2001||09:58 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JayUSA77:<BR><B>hey guess what guys i was talking to my shop teacher and he said the reason they made the GT slower than what it could of been is because the guys making the Corvette were getting nervous on how it might step on the toes of the corvette for far less than the price.  Aint that something.<BR>J<BR>While the shop teacher is accurate in his statement, the fact of the matter is that Pontiac Motor Division had a least a dozen Fiero V8's running at the GM Proving Grounds (cars were were converted to V8's with the old Gary Zumalt Kit by Pontiac). Pontiac wanted to save the Fiero by offering a "hot model", which car publications had hoped Pontiac would produce. Trouble started in the '86 - '87 timeframe when these cars were outperforming the corvettes in all areas of performance. Chevrolet/Corvette Group stepped in and was effective in putting the whole program in the dumpster. Strong internal rumor at GM is that Chevrolet gave Pontiac numerous concessions not to produce the V8 powered Fiero. They also had some twin turbo V6 prototypes (not 2.8) that wipped the vettes also, that they weren't allowed to produce.<BR>Tom<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_7.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by California Kid (edited 09-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Master_Sushi||09-23-2001||10:37 AM||||I also think they probably just cheaped out. My father use to work for GM and you wouldnt beleave the stories of cheapness I heard. They are terrable, saving pennies on each car built in exchange for putting in crap parts. Its the same with most big businesses now though.||||reg||13
Z||000006||Tonker||09-23-2001||01:14 PM||||This is exactly why I will never again buy a GM product - and to date GM is the only brand I've ever owned (it's all my parents have bought since I've been alive too). Who the hell are they to tell me what I want? They aren't here to produce what Chevy wants, they're here to produce what the customer wants.<P>My resolve is helped a great deal by all the ugly shite being produced by GM these days.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||13
Z||000007||JayUSA77||09-23-2001||01:31 PM||||ya that does suck how GM got cheap but then if you look at it its still better than ford.  Wanna know something really funny about ford. There fastest production vehicle is a truck. The lighting. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||Wannabe||09-23-2001||02:19 PM||||GM - "General Mayhem" I've always found GM's products to be great in concept, poor in excecution - although there have been notable exceptions when they've had enough time to get it right.||||reg||1
Z||000009||terryk||09-23-2001||04:13 PM||||Wow! They detuned the 2.8L V6 engine to keep the power below the 5.7L V8? <P>Those ba$tards!<P>I can appreciate the thought, but the P car chassis was never intended to handle the power of an engine that would make it faster than a Vette.<P>The Fiero's marketting segment was not to be the top power car in the GM line-up. <P>This same argument could be used to support a conspiracy against the Chevette engineers (Corvette was afraid).<P>Think about it this way, if the Fiero engineer's were allowed to do something to make the Fiero as fast as a Vette, just how much effort would it take for the Vette engineers to go faster? Not much. The Vette chassis was designed to handle the larger engines. The Fiero wasn't.<P>The bottom line is that *we* picked a car that wasn't intended to be blazingly fast. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||California Kid||09-23-2001||05:22 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by terryk:<BR><B>Think about it this way, if the Fiero engineer's were allowed to do something to make the Fiero as fast as a Vette, just how much effort would it take for the Vette engineers to go faster? Not much. The Vette chassis was designed to handle the larger engines. The Fiero wasn't.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>What you may not be aware of is that the Fiero, at the time of design, was designed to take any engine that was in the GM inventory at that time, that's why even "Big Block" engines with fit in it. The Fiero Chassis is the strongest ever made by GM, with exception maybe to the newer C5 Vette. Weight distribution isn't a problem either, my GT350 carries 55% on rear tires and 45% up front which makes it almost perfect. Suspension upgrades aren't expensive to attain performance better than the vette, and the weight advantage is in the Fiero's favor. If Pontiac had gotten their way, the Corvette today would be like Ford's T-Bird.<P>Just some thoughts.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_7.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by California Kid (edited 09-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||rockcrawl||09-23-2001||06:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>was designed to take any engine that was in the GM inventory at that time, that's why even "Big Block" engines with fit in it<HR></BLOCKQUOTE> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||DreXteR||09-23-2001||07:00 PM||||Grr.. Bin Laden should crash the planes in the GM head quaters..  heheehhe  j/k<P>DreX||||reg||10
Z||000013||Sage||09-23-2001||07:34 PM||||A friend of mine who used own and operate a Corvette shop, told me some years ago that he got to drive an 88' Fiero owned by a Pontiac dealer CEO.  He said it had a twin turbo 3800 in it with a five speed.  Claimed that it would have blown the doors off any big block Vette that he had ever driven.  Said the A-arms were tubular and the brake calipers were on the opposite side of the rotors compared to a stock Fiero.  Calif. Kid: Yours is the first mention, (other than my friend), I've ever heard of the "twin turbo" 3800 in a factory Fiero.  He says the car looked stock in every other way, except he said it had "special badging"<P>Any thoughts-knowledge on this?<P><BR>Have a good one!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
